      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "https://www.data4thepeople.com/p/beyond-the-unemployment-rate/#dataset",
      "name": "CPS Monthly Explorer: Published Current Population Survey Series by Dimension, Group, and Measure, 1948 to Present",
      "alternateName": [
        "Beyond the Unemployment Rate",
        "CPS Data Explorer",
        "BLS Current Population Survey Explorer"
      ],
      "description": "An interactive explorer over 2,151 published series from the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics Current Population Survey time series database (LN), covering 33 measures across 21 demographic and labor-market breakdowns and 188 groups, monthly from January 1948. Measures include the civilian labor force, employment, unemployment, the unemployment rate, the labor force participation rate, the employment-population ratio, the number not in the labor force, the civilian noninstitutional population, part-time and full-time employment, duration of unemployment, and the monthly labor force flows between employment, unemployment and not-in-labor-force. Breakdowns include age, activity, class of worker, disability status, duration of unemployment, education, hispanic origin, industry, job seeker status, labor force entrant, marital status, multiple jobholders, nativity, occupation, race, reason for unemployment, sex, veteran status, want a job, work experience, and work schedule status. Every view is a single official BLS series, identified by joining the ln.series catalog to its companion code-mapping files. No values are summed, averaged across series, estimated or modeled, and the underlying BLS series ID is displayed under each chart so any figure can be verified against bls.gov.",
      "url": "https://www.data4thepeople.com/p/beyond-the-unemployment-rate/",
      "sameAs": "https://github.com/Data4ThePeople/CPS_monthly_explorer",
      "license": "https://www.data4thepeople.com/terms-of-use",
      "isAccessibleForFree": true,
      "temporalCoverage": "1948-01-01/..",
